    }
  ],
  "seo": {
    "title": "How to Lower Blood Pressure Naturally",
    "description": "Discover evidence-backed daily habits to help lower high blood pressure, including diet changes, exercise, sleep, and knowing when to see a doctor."
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "How quickly do lifestyle changes lower blood pressure?",
      "answer": "Noticeable shifts in blood pressure readings often begin appearing within two to four weeks of consistent dietary changes and regular exercise, though long-term maintenance is essential for sustained results."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does drinking more water lower blood pressure?",
      "answer": "Adequate hydration helps maintain healthy blood volume and kidney function, but drinking excess water does not directly treat high blood pressure; balanced salt intake and overall diet play a much larger role."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can walking alone help bring blood pressure down?",
      "answer": "Yes. Brisk walking for 30 minutes on most days is one of the most thoroughly researched and effective forms of aerobic exercise for supporting lower blood pressure."
    }
  ]
